==Reactions==
* {{Flag|Argentina}}: President [[Javier Milei]] congratulated both Rodrigo Paz and the Bolivian people on his election victory, and stating that Bolivia "left behind 20 years of the failed model that was [[socialism of the 21st century]]".<ref>{{Cite web |date=20 October 2025 |title=Milei felicitó a Rodrigo Paz por el triunfo en Bolivia: "Esta jornada democrática refleja el anhelo de libertad" |url=https://www.lanacion.com.ar/politica/milei-felicito-a-rodrigo-paz-por-el-triunfo-en-bolivia-esta-jornada-democratica-refleja-el-anhelo-de-nid20102025/ |access-date=22 October 2025 |website=La Nación (Argentina) |language=es}}</ref>
* {{Flag|Brazil}}: President [[Lula da Silva]] congratulated Rodrigo Paz on his election victory, and talked about preserving [[Bolivia–Brazil relations|relations]] between Bolivia and Brazil.<ref>{{Cite web |date=20 October 2025 |title=Lula parabeniza Rodrigo Paz por eleição na Bolívia e fala em "cooperação" |url=https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/politica/lula-parabeniza-rodrigo-paz-por-eleicao-na-bolivia-e-fala-em-cooperacao/ |access-date=22 October 2025 |website=CNN Brasil |language=pt}}</ref>
* {{Flag|Chile}}: President [[Gabriel Boric]] congratulated Rodrigo Paz on his election victory, reaffirming Chile's "commitment to strengthening cooperation and joint work between brotherly nations for the benefit of our peoples." Boric also praised the Bolivian people for their participation in the runoff between Paz and Quiroga.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ovalle |first=Christian |date=20 October 2025 |title=Boric felicita a presidente electo de Bolivia Rodrigo Paz y reafirma compromiso de trabajo conjunto |url=https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/nacional/chile/2025/10/20/boric-felicita-a-presidente-electo-de-bolivia-rodrigo-paz-y-reafirma-compromiso-de-trabajo-conjunto.shtml |access-date=22 October 2025 |website=BioBioChile – La Red de Prensa Más Grande de Chile |language=es}}</ref>
* {{Flag|Israel}}: Foreign minister [[Gideon Sa'ar]] congratulated Rodrigo Paz, stating that Bolivia and Israel will "turn a new page and fully renew [[Bolivia–Israel relations|diplomatic relations]] between the countries". Relations between the two countries were strained since the start of the [[Gaza war]] in 2023.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.ynetnews.com/article/bjhwqfvaxg |last=Eichner |first=Itamar |publisher=[[Ynet]] |date=20 October 2025 |accessdate=21 October 2025 |language=en |title=Bolivia is ready to renew relations with Israel: 'A new page'}}</ref>
* {{Flag|Paraguay}}: President [[Santiago Peña]] congratulated Rodrigo Paz on his election win, and emphasized the "brotherly [[Bolivia–Paraguay relations|ties]]" between Bolivia and Paraguay.<ref>{{cite web|access-date=21 October 2025 |date=20 October 2025 |language=es |title=Peña felicita a Paz por triunfo en Bolivia y ve ocasión de fortalecer "lazos de hermandad" |url=https://www.swissinfo.ch/spa/pe%C3%B1a-felicita-a-paz-por-triunfo-en-bolivia-y-ve-ocasi%C3%B3n-de-fortalecer-%22lazos-de-hermandad%22/90196691 |website=SWI}}<!-- auto-translated from Spanish by Module:CS1 translator --></ref>
* {{Flag|Peru}}: President [[José Jeri]] congratulated Rodrigo Paz, and stated that the [[Bolivia–Peru relations|relations]] between the two countries are a "priority".<ref>{{Cite news|title=El presidente del Perú José Jerí felicita al presidente electo de Bolivia, Rodrigo Paz, y propone retomar diálogo al más alto nivel|url=https://www.infobae.com/peru/2025/10/20/jose-jeri-felicita-al-presidente-electo-de-bolivia-rodrigo-paz-y-propone-retomar-dialogo-al-mas-alto-nivel/|date=20 October 2025|access-date=20 October 2025|publisher=infobae.com}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|title=Presidente José Jerí Oré felicita al nuevo presidente de Bolivia por su triunfo en la segunda vuelta electoral|url=https://www.gob.pe/institucion/presidencia/noticias/1268649-presidente-jose-jeri-ore-felicita-al-nuevo-presidente-de-bolivia-por-su-triunfo-en-la-segunda-vuelta-electoral|date=19 October 2025|access-date=20 October 2025|publisher=gob.pe}}</ref>
* {{Flag|United States}}: Secretary of State [[Marco Rubio]] congratulated Rodrigo Paz saying that his victory marks the end of nearly two decades of "government mismanagement and bad governance in Bolivia" and also pledged to work with the incoming Bolivian administration to help them [[War on drugs|fight against drug cartels and criminal gangs]].{{citation needed|date=October 2025}} Shortly before the second round of elections, Rubio said on 15 October 2025 that the two leading candidates (Libre and the PDC), "[[Bolivia–United States relations|want better relations with the United States]] after years of [[Anti-Americanism|anti-American]] leadership in Bolivia" and also said that the election would be a "transformative opportunity'.<ref name="runoffresults"/>

